{"kind":"artifact","text":"Answers changes-requested verdict dd85f77f on 69f78d37. Part one of the kernel admission gaps: rests_on resolvability. internal/kernel refuses a genuinely new submission whose rests_on carries a canonical event identifier for this log that names no position in it, with ErrUnresolvedReference naming the reference. Submit now runs the idempotency lookup first and returns the replay or conflict before resolving references, so an exact retry of a historical record whose bases dangle replays that record, consistent with Verify and Load, which read history as written. A reference that makes no claim about this log is carried unchanged. Resolution reads the Positions commit index maintained beside the dedup index on every path that builds one: cold scan, streamed delta, full and compact checkpoint restore (retained and streamed), and local append; the check asks Git nothing. Tests in internal/kernel/references_test.go: TestSubmitRefusesFabricatedInLogReference, TestSubmitterRefusesFabricatedInLogReference, TestSubmitAdmitsResolvedInLogReferences, TestSubmitRefusesSelfReference, TestSubmitRefusesCommitOutsideTheLog, TestSubmitCarriesReferencesItCannotResolve, and TestVerifyAcceptsHistoricalDanglingReference, which now retries the historical record and wants a replay. Mutation-checked at this head: disabling the Positions check fails the four refusal tests; restoring the old check-before-dedup ordering fails the retry with ErrUnresolvedReference. Gates at this exact head: gofmt, git diff --check and go vet clean; go test -count=1 -race ./internal/kernel green; go test -count=1 ./... green in all 27 packages including the docset citation gate.","body":{"commit":"637506e39770f0f102691342395ef132c16121c3","path":"internal/kernel"}}